    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The fix is complete! Here's what I changed:\n\n**Problem:** When parsing \"39.95\" to cents, the code was doing `Number(39.95) * 100`, which resulted in `3995.0000000000005` due to floating-point precision errors. The validation then rejected this because it's not an integer.\n\n**Solution:** In `src/money.js`, I rewrote both `parseEuros` and `cellCents` to parse the string directly to cents by splitting on the decimal point and handling the integer and decimal parts separately. This avoids any floating-point intermediate values.\n\n**Testing:** \n- All existing tests pass \u2705\n- `39.95` now correctly converts to exactly `3995` cents (verified above)\n- `12.99` \u2192 `1299` cents \u2705\n- `10.99` \u2192 `1099` cents \u2705\n\nThe code is ready to commit. Would you like me to commit this fix?",
